## Recovery Contract

- Missing, multiple, or cyclic parentage is surfaced under Needs placement and never guessed.
- Narrowing retains context ancestors and never reports them as matching remaining work.
- Reporter or hosted-version incompatibility keeps the release chain open and visibly stale.
- Failed platform, CI, release, deployment, or convergence evidence leaves the owning outcome open.

## Verification Strategy

- Unit-test membership, placement, cycles, ordering, filtering, ancestry, whole-root pagination,
  Next selection, allowlisted commands, clipboard fallback, and accessible interaction.
- Exercise malformed and multi-linked synthetic trees without duplicating or silently placing rows.
- Run strict Doctor, the full repository validator, development web checks, clean and upgraded
  Linux and Windows qualification, exact-SHA CI, release provenance, production deployment, and a
  fresh report whose hosted page renders the current IDEA-0023 chain immediately.
